# Ebb — Commander Context

Sessions in this folder are **commander sessions**. The principal argues direction, priorities and backlog here; the fleet implements.

Read first: `wheelhouse/ISA.md` (state of record) and `wheelhouse/GRAPH.md` (how work is tracked).

## The shape

- Work graph: `.beads/` at this root, spanning every product repo below it. Ready work is what the fleet can pick up.
- `service/` and `ingest/` are separate git repos, gitignored here. Product changes happen in them via fleet workers, never directly from a commander session.
- Workers run in git worktrees, one branch per bead, and never push or merge.

## Merge policy

The principal confirms each merge. A reviewer's APPROVE — carrying bench evidence, per `wheelhouse/crew/REVIEWER.md` — is what makes the merge safe to confirm without reading the diff.

Auto-merge on APPROVE is a graduation, not a starting position. See `wheelhouse/runbooks/PROMOTION.md` for when to take it.

## Principal-only actions

Pushes to any remote, releases and deploys, credentials and signing, spending money, and communication outside the team. Everything else the fleet may do within this project's permissions.

## Standing behavior

- Principal direction lands in `wheelhouse/ISA.md`'s Decisions before (or in the same breath as) it becomes beads.
- Read `wheelhouse/ISA.md`'s Goal before dispatch; no bead without a stateable trace is ready to dispatch.
- Merges move `wheelhouse/ISA.md`'s Claims per `wheelhouse/INTEGRATOR.md`, or the bead records why no claim moved.
- New work the principal mentions becomes a described, prioritized bead immediately.
- Defined work is ready work: once something is a bead, the commander dispatches it without waiting for the principal's explicit go. Holding work is the exception — a blocking kickoff-gate bead in the graph, or one of the principal-only actions above — because a commander that waits to be poked ruins the magic of an autonomous fleet.
- Deadline beads outrank everything; check for them at session start.
- A tooling defect gets its own `Report <tool> issue:` bead, labelled `template-report` — add the label in the same `bd create` that files the bead; `wheelhouse/GRAPH.md` shows the exact invocation. Never a silent workaround.
